# Integrity-hashed surfaces must be byte-identical across platforms. The leak-guard
# (tests/test_tb_leak_guard.py) and the prospective-lock manifests sha256-pin these files;
# a Windows CRLF checkout would drift the hash vs a Linux/CI LF checkout. Force LF so the
# pinned hash is stable everywhere. (Root-caused 2026-06-27: calibrated_amr_rules.json was
# CRLF locally / LF in the repo blob -> CI hash mismatch on the frozen-surface gate.)
dna_decode/eval/amr_rules.py            text eol=lf
dna_decode/data/calibrated_amr_rules.json text eol=lf
dna_decode/data/mic_tiers.py            text eol=lf
dna_decode/data/shipped_decoder_surface.py text eol=lf
dna_decode/eval/cohort_manifest.py      text eol=lf
dna_decode/data/sarscov2_amr.py         text eol=lf
scripts/sarscov2_caller.py              text eol=lf

# Integrity-pinned DATA. `data/raw/tb_lineage_barcode/CHECKSUMS` pins the UPSTREAM
# (tbdb commit 618cf0ff) sha256, which is the LF digest -- so a Windows CRLF checkout
# fails the pin with 'barcode drift' when not one character has changed. Measured
# 2026-10-19: on-disk CRLF hashed f8357f509e7a, LF-normalised 9c0567304561, and the pin
# is 9c0567304561. Third instance of this class in one day (the other two: the frozen
# AMR surface above, and wiki/provdisjoint_lineage_metrics.json, whose scorer was taught
# to compare EOL renderings because its bar is a frozen pre-commitment that must not be
# edited). Only genuinely TEXT files belong here: `data/` also holds .gz/.zip/.xlsx/.docx
# /.pdf whose compressed bytes contain 0d0a, and declaring those `text` would CORRUPT
# them on checkout -- git already auto-detects them as binary (verified: on-disk size ==
# blob size after a restore).
data/raw/tb_lineage_barcode/barcode.bed text eol=lf
